1
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:41,959
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:57,512 --> 00:00:59,430
That's my house right there.

3
00:00:59,722 --> 00:01:00,806
It's late. You should go home.

4
00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:02,350
But we're almost there.
Why would you...

5
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,643
I'll walk you to your house.

6
00:01:03,851 --> 00:01:05,937
No need,
thank you for walking me home.

7
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:08,689
You should go home. Thank you.

8
00:01:10,608 --> 00:01:12,151
It's slippery.

9
00:01:12,235 --> 00:01:13,569
- If you don't watch out...
- Mr. Kang!

10
00:01:35,216 --> 00:01:38,970
I was worried you'd end up hurt
if you weren't careful.

11
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:45,434
If anything...

12
00:01:48,271 --> 00:01:49,647
this seems more dangerous.

13
00:01:55,361 --> 00:01:56,362
I'm sorry.

14
00:01:59,490 --> 00:02:01,492
I should get going.

15
00:02:01,576 --> 00:02:03,995
Take care on your way home. Goodbye.

16
00:02:22,722 --> 00:02:24,765
{\an8}EPISODE 3

17
00:02:36,235 --> 00:02:37,695
{\an8}This seems more dangerous.

18
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:47,079
{\an8}I did save him from danger...

19
00:02:48,956 --> 00:02:51,292
{\an8}but did I offend him somehow?

20
00:02:52,627 --> 00:02:54,378
{\an8}Still, I saved his life.

21
00:02:54,837 --> 00:02:56,380
{\an8}He was being too cold.

22
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:35,461
<i>Ms. Nam!</i>

23
00:03:41,008 --> 00:03:43,719
No.

24
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,722
<i>Mr. Kang!</i>

25
00:03:47,348 --> 00:03:50,768
<i>I was worried you'd end up hurt
if you weren't careful.</i>

26
00:03:58,901 --> 00:03:59,944
What's this?

27
00:04:02,113 --> 00:04:03,239
What's wrong with my heart?

28
00:04:05,741 --> 00:04:06,867
Do I have a heart problem?

29
00:04:07,535 --> 00:04:10,746
Mr. Kang, have this and cheer up.

30
00:04:11,956 --> 00:04:12,957
Good luck.

31
00:04:13,916 --> 00:04:16,085
<i>Mr. Kang, do you drink coffee now?</i>

32
00:04:16,168 --> 00:04:18,921
I thought you didn't drink coffee.
What's gotten into you?

33
00:04:19,338 --> 00:04:20,589
<i>Coffee...</i>

34
00:04:21,549 --> 00:04:22,550
Right.

35
00:04:23,259 --> 00:04:24,510
It's the coffee.

36
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:30,391
I shouldn't have had it.

37
00:04:33,644 --> 00:04:35,104
It's just the coffee.

38
00:05:08,929 --> 00:05:11,849
Appello.

39
00:05:13,768 --> 00:05:18,606
The Outstanding Employee
of the Year is...

40
00:05:19,273 --> 00:05:20,316
Gosh, it's nerve-wracking.

41
00:05:21,984 --> 00:05:23,235
The winner is...

42
00:05:27,448 --> 00:05:28,616
Congratulations.

43
00:05:29,325 --> 00:05:32,244
It goes to...

44
00:05:32,328 --> 00:05:33,662
Me?

45
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,207
Me?

46
00:05:36,832 --> 00:05:37,833
Come on.

47
00:05:44,507 --> 00:05:45,549
Kang...

48
00:05:47,384 --> 00:05:48,469
Ha...

49
00:05:49,678 --> 00:05:50,846
Gi!

50
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:53,641
KANG HA-GI

51
00:05:58,979 --> 00:06:00,731
No way.

52
00:06:07,238 --> 00:06:09,406
{\an8}FLIGHT TICKET TO NEW YORK

53
00:06:16,038 --> 00:06:17,540
No...

54
00:06:18,415 --> 00:06:19,667
This can't be true.

55
00:06:20,751 --> 00:06:21,836
What...

56
00:06:23,045 --> 00:06:24,213
Wait!

57
00:06:25,506 --> 00:06:29,426
Mr. Kang, you're the CEO.
You can't pick yourself.

58
00:06:32,596 --> 00:06:34,223
I'm also an employee of Appello.

59
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:36,225
That's still not fair.

60
00:06:37,226 --> 00:06:39,228
You know how hard I worked.

61
00:06:39,395 --> 00:06:40,813
I worked harder.

62
00:06:41,939 --> 00:06:44,108
You shouldn't abuse your power
for personal gain like this.

63
00:06:46,944 --> 00:06:47,945
What did you say?

64
00:06:48,571 --> 00:06:49,613
"Personal gain"?

65
00:06:53,617 --> 00:06:55,995
Ms. Nam, how much do you know?

66
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:57,705
No, I...

67
00:06:58,205 --> 00:07:00,416
- The thing is...
- Actually, forget it.

68
00:07:01,667 --> 00:07:03,878
As of this moment, you're fired.

69
00:07:05,045 --> 00:07:06,046
What?

70
00:07:06,755 --> 00:07:08,841
I said you're fired.

71
00:07:08,924 --> 00:07:10,676
You're fired.

72
00:07:10,759 --> 00:07:14,305
No!

73
00:07:14,388 --> 00:07:15,514
No!

74
00:07:25,482 --> 00:07:26,609
What was that?

75
00:07:27,526 --> 00:07:28,986
A premonition?

76
00:07:29,403 --> 00:07:31,780
No, no way.

77
00:07:33,657 --> 00:07:35,701
It was just a meaningless dream.

78
00:07:39,538 --> 00:07:40,623
What on earth?

79
00:07:49,548 --> 00:07:50,633
What's with the weather?

80
00:07:55,721 --> 00:07:57,723
Man, things are flying everywhere.

81
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,188
Our stage!

82
00:08:05,856 --> 00:08:08,067
We've got unexpected heavy rain.

83
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:10,986
Roads are closed,
and the winds are out of control.

84
00:08:12,029 --> 00:08:14,031
The brand CEOs might have
a hard time making it.

85
00:08:14,114 --> 00:08:16,075
Right, we'll probably be
the first to arrive.

86
00:08:16,158 --> 00:08:18,077
How bad is the damage?
Do we have confirmation yet?

87
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,204
I'm afraid we won't know for sure
until we see it in person.

88
00:08:52,736 --> 00:08:53,779
Mr. Kang.

89
00:08:54,446 --> 00:08:56,407
Get the security personnel
in place first.

90
00:08:57,199 --> 00:08:59,910
Tie down or clear out any equipment
that might shift or fall.

91
00:09:00,244 --> 00:09:01,245
Yes, sir.

92
00:09:02,287 --> 00:09:03,706
Wait. Mr. Kang.

93
00:09:18,971 --> 00:09:20,889
Who already did all this?

94
00:09:21,682 --> 00:09:22,766
Mr. Kang.

95
00:09:22,850 --> 00:09:25,477
Someone covered everything
with tarps here too.

96
00:09:29,898 --> 00:09:31,650
The CEOs haven't arrived yet,
have they?

97
00:09:31,942 --> 00:09:34,820
Yes, who could've done all this?

98
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:41,452
Wait. Mr. Kang, isn't that...

99
00:09:46,081 --> 00:09:47,249
Who's that over there?

100
00:09:49,710 --> 00:09:50,794
Mr. Kang.

101
00:09:56,050 --> 00:09:57,134
Hello?

102
00:09:57,468 --> 00:09:58,594
You've arrived?

103
00:09:58,802 --> 00:10:00,512
Wait there for a moment.

104
00:10:26,914 --> 00:10:29,541
Mr. Kang, the employees have arrived.

105
00:10:29,625 --> 00:10:31,335
I'll be right back. Please wait here.

106
00:10:49,394 --> 00:10:50,646
I have to save the clothes at least.

107
00:10:58,821 --> 00:10:59,947
Ms. Nam?

108
00:11:01,615 --> 00:11:03,951
Mr. Kang, you're here.

109
00:11:04,034 --> 00:11:06,578
- What are you doing here alone?
- Oh, the clothes.

110
00:11:06,662 --> 00:11:08,288
They're the vendors' assets.

111
00:11:08,372 --> 00:11:09,873
I'm trying to salvage what I can.

112
00:11:15,003 --> 00:11:16,213
Jeez.

113
00:11:17,548 --> 00:11:19,633
Do you realize
how dangerous it is out here?

114
00:11:20,008 --> 00:11:21,218
Why would you be here alone?

115
00:11:22,344 --> 00:11:24,263
I'm sorry. I was in a rush.

116
00:11:24,346 --> 00:11:27,057
Let's wrap this up fast
and get somewhere safe.

117
00:11:27,558 --> 00:11:28,559
Okay.

118
00:11:40,362 --> 00:11:41,446
No!

119
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,002
It's dangerous. Stay away, Ms. Nam.

120
00:11:55,961 --> 00:11:57,129
Let's do this together.

121
00:11:57,212 --> 00:11:58,213
Move over there.

122
00:11:58,297 --> 00:12:00,132
Now that we're holding it together

123
00:12:00,632 --> 00:12:02,176
it's not shaking anymore.

124
00:12:06,847 --> 00:12:09,892
Look, the wind is dying down.

125
00:12:10,267 --> 00:12:11,935
I'm sure the rain will stop soon too.

126
00:12:13,645 --> 00:12:15,105
Let's cheer up just a bit more.

127
00:12:20,611 --> 00:12:21,612
How can you be

128
00:12:22,821 --> 00:12:23,864
smiling at a time like this?

129
00:12:24,072 --> 00:12:25,949
You've got to smile
when things get tough.

130
00:12:26,491 --> 00:12:27,784
Don't you know

131
00:12:28,827 --> 00:12:30,829
smiling actually makes things better?

132
00:13:00,984 --> 00:13:02,945
Mr. Kang, we're here.

133
00:13:03,153 --> 00:13:05,697
Let me put this on you.

134
00:13:14,373 --> 00:13:15,374
Good.

135
00:13:15,916 --> 00:13:16,917
Two, three.

136
00:13:19,628 --> 00:13:21,129
Here. Enjoy.

137
00:13:21,255 --> 00:13:22,631
- Have some bread while you work.
- Okay.

138
00:13:24,967 --> 00:13:26,051
Does this need to go up?

139
00:13:27,135 --> 00:13:28,887
Should we set it up? Two, three.

140
00:13:28,971 --> 00:13:31,056
Press it down. One, two, three.

141
00:13:32,182 --> 00:13:34,101
Don't put yourself in danger
like that again.

142
00:13:34,685 --> 00:13:36,061
Safety comes first.

143
00:13:38,522 --> 00:13:39,564
Yes, sir.

144
00:13:41,858 --> 00:13:43,068
Still, I do...

145
00:13:45,237 --> 00:13:46,280
appreciate your intentions.

146
00:13:47,239 --> 00:13:48,240
Excuse me?

147
00:13:48,782 --> 00:13:50,242
- What did you just say?
- I mean...

148
00:13:52,869 --> 00:13:55,122
Nothing. I'm just saying.

149
00:14:01,295 --> 00:14:02,337
Is everything okay?

150
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:04,506
It's delicious.

151
00:14:04,589 --> 00:14:08,135
Maybe because it's soaked in tears...
I mean, rainwater.

152
00:14:08,969 --> 00:14:10,304
No, I didn't mean that bread.

153
00:14:14,266 --> 00:14:15,392
Never mind.

154
00:14:52,804 --> 00:14:53,972
- Careful.
- Okay.

155
00:14:54,056 --> 00:14:56,058
It's not exactly
that we're canceling.

156
00:14:56,516 --> 00:14:57,768
If you could just
give us some time...

157
00:14:57,851 --> 00:14:58,852
No, that's enough.

158
00:14:58,935 --> 00:15:00,937
We'll consider this discussion over.

159
00:15:01,021 --> 00:15:02,773
- But...
- Sir, you can't leave like this.

160
00:15:03,231 --> 00:15:05,484
Sir. Ma'am. Wait.

161
00:15:05,942 --> 00:15:07,694
- We're done.
- Wait.

162
00:15:10,322 --> 00:15:11,490
What's going on?

163
00:15:11,698 --> 00:15:14,076
BRB backed out of the contract.

164
00:15:14,659 --> 00:15:16,161
So did Saucebody, Sweetheart

165
00:15:16,703 --> 00:15:17,746
and 9203 too.

166
00:15:19,581 --> 00:15:21,708
I personally called the CEOs
not to worry.

167
00:15:21,792 --> 00:15:23,752
They somehow heard a rumor

168
00:15:23,835 --> 00:15:25,379
about the Appello fashion show
getting canceled

169
00:15:25,462 --> 00:15:27,005
and came to see for themselves.

170
00:15:27,714 --> 00:15:28,840
Looks like

171
00:15:28,924 --> 00:15:31,051
SE leaked some info.

172
00:15:31,468 --> 00:15:32,969
They're signing with SE instead.

173
00:15:37,349 --> 00:15:39,893
Unless our information is sent to SE
in real time

174
00:15:39,976 --> 00:15:41,603
it's hard to find out.

175
00:15:41,686 --> 00:15:44,564
Sir, you don't think the spy is...

176
00:15:50,904 --> 00:15:53,281
Would a spy be out here
since dawn working that hard?

177
00:15:53,365 --> 00:15:56,660
Being here since dawn means
they could get the info faster.

178
00:16:03,583 --> 00:16:06,211
- Gosh. Mr. Young-woo, this.
- Okay.

179
00:16:06,711 --> 00:16:07,796
Here you go.

180
00:16:08,922 --> 00:16:11,967
Clear things up here.
I think it's pretty much done.

181
00:16:12,426 --> 00:16:13,552
I'm going elsewhere.

182
00:16:13,635 --> 00:16:15,053
Finish that up.

183
00:16:16,596 --> 00:16:18,056
I can't believe
all this is going to waste.

184
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:20,725
At least we managed
to salvage these clothes.

185
00:16:21,101 --> 00:16:22,644
Everyone worked so hard
on preparing this.

186
00:16:37,492 --> 00:16:38,577
Sir.

187
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,121
Are you okay?

188
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,251
I heard

189
00:16:46,334 --> 00:16:49,087
you salvaged our clothes
by covering them with tarps.

190
00:16:49,337 --> 00:16:50,672
Thank you so much.

191
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:57,053
What happens to those clothes now?

192
00:16:59,097 --> 00:17:01,933
They were meant for on-site sales
at the fashion show.

193
00:17:03,268 --> 00:17:04,769
I suppose
they'll just sit in inventory.

194
00:17:11,151 --> 00:17:14,529
It's ending
before I even get started.

195
00:17:16,406 --> 00:17:17,699
I haven't given up yet.

196
00:17:21,495 --> 00:17:22,537
Excuse me?

197
00:17:22,621 --> 00:17:24,706
It's not over until it's truly over.

198
00:17:25,165 --> 00:17:27,792
Will you trust me
and follow my lead one last time?

199
00:17:37,969 --> 00:17:42,599
Guys, the moment you've all been
waiting for is finally here.

200
00:17:42,682 --> 00:17:44,976
For today's <i>Morning Greetings</i>...

201
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:49,314
I actually took a shower this morning
because of this guest.

202
00:17:49,397 --> 00:17:52,651
It's the busiest actor
and fashion director these days.

203
00:17:52,984 --> 00:17:55,779
His name literally means "Two cold."
It's Lee Chan. Welcome.

204
00:17:56,112 --> 00:17:58,240
Two, three. We're destiny.

205
00:17:58,323 --> 00:18:00,825
Hello, I'm Lee Chan from D.N.X.
It's nice to meet you.

206
00:18:00,909 --> 00:18:02,118
DJ AN YOUNG-MI

207
00:18:02,202 --> 00:18:04,454
You're still using that greeting?

208
00:18:04,913 --> 00:18:06,957
You've been using it
since you debuted as an idol, right?

209
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:10,043
Right. But since no one
calls me that anymore

210
00:18:10,126 --> 00:18:12,379
I keep it alive myself.

211
00:18:12,462 --> 00:18:16,758
Do you ever find yourself
wanting to go back

212
00:18:16,841 --> 00:18:18,385
to your D.N.X days?

213
00:18:18,468 --> 00:18:19,511
Of course.

214
00:18:19,844 --> 00:18:22,847
I know a lot of fans are
still waiting.

215
00:18:22,931 --> 00:18:25,433
How are the other members
doing lately?

216
00:18:28,687 --> 00:18:31,147
They all seem to be doing well
in their own lanes.

217
00:18:32,566 --> 00:18:36,861
We always talk about reuniting
someday for sure.

218
00:18:37,487 --> 00:18:41,408
Really? That's going to be
great news for your fans.

219
00:18:42,576 --> 00:18:45,036
On that note, our first song today

220
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:50,500
will be <i>Dear My Light</i>
from D.N.X's final album.

221
00:18:51,626 --> 00:18:53,169
- Oh, my.
- Jeez.

222
00:18:53,628 --> 00:18:55,922
Are you out of your mind?
How can you hide something like this?

223
00:18:56,256 --> 00:18:58,049
- Calm down.
- Chan.

224
00:18:58,133 --> 00:18:59,467
You can't do this here!

225
00:18:59,551 --> 00:19:00,802
What is it? Say something.

226
00:19:00,885 --> 00:19:02,679
- Get off me!
- Calm down already.

227
00:19:02,762 --> 00:19:03,805
Come on.

228
00:19:05,181 --> 00:19:07,100
- Hey.
- Get off!

229
00:19:07,434 --> 00:19:09,477
- Hey.
- Don't do this to Roy.

230
00:19:09,853 --> 00:19:11,354
- Stop.
- Move. Get out of my way!

231
00:19:11,438 --> 00:19:13,315
- Don't do this too.
- I said, move!

232
00:19:18,570 --> 00:19:19,696
You're no different.

233
00:19:20,739 --> 00:19:23,116
The two of you ruined
everything we built!

234
00:19:52,103 --> 00:19:53,688
{\an8}ROY, LEAVE THE GROUP

235
00:19:53,772 --> 00:19:58,193
{\an8}D.N.X OFFICIALLY ANNOUNCES DISBANDING

236
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:16,711
Hey.

237
00:20:47,575 --> 00:20:48,993
I'm just getting better at lying.

238
00:20:49,619 --> 00:20:51,496
What was that?

239
00:20:52,414 --> 00:20:54,457
No, nothing.

240
00:21:02,424 --> 00:21:03,758
{\an8}I CRIED SO MUCH TODAY, BUT I'M FINE

241
00:21:05,552 --> 00:21:07,554
{\an8}THESE AREN'T TEARS OF SADNESS
BUT SUPPORT FOR YOUR NEW START

242
00:21:07,637 --> 00:21:09,389
{\an8}I BELIEVE I'LL GET TO SEE YOU
SHINE ON STAGE AGAIN

243
00:21:16,479 --> 00:21:19,441
What? What exactly do you mean, sir?

244
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:21,109
The Appello fashion show

245
00:21:21,401 --> 00:21:22,944
- will proceed tomorrow as planned.
- What?

246
00:21:23,027 --> 00:21:25,947
We already took a big loss. Are you
suggesting we rebuild the stage?

247
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:28,074
Yes, we must do it.

248
00:21:28,825 --> 00:21:31,453
If the participating brands suffer,
who'd ever want to partner with us?

249
00:21:32,370 --> 00:21:33,747
If we lose them here...

250
00:21:36,791 --> 00:21:38,752
losing the market to SE will only be

251
00:21:40,503 --> 00:21:41,629
a matter of time.

252
00:21:46,885 --> 00:21:48,845
Is there even a place
we can use right away?

253
00:21:49,763 --> 00:21:50,889
Right here.

254
00:21:52,891 --> 00:21:54,517
- Here?
- Yes.

255
00:21:55,435 --> 00:21:57,812
- We'll do an online show.
- What?

256
00:22:03,985 --> 00:22:05,403
We'll use this space as the runway.

257
00:22:05,779 --> 00:22:07,238
We'll set up four stationary cameras

258
00:22:07,405 --> 00:22:09,073
and focus on the looks
against a white backdrop.

259
00:22:09,157 --> 00:22:11,743
Given how small the space is,
won't it look a bit too plain?

260
00:22:11,993 --> 00:22:13,495
The clothes might actually
stand out more.

261
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:17,707
Our whole thing was an open-air show
accessible to everyone.

262
00:22:17,791 --> 00:22:18,875
It's such a shame.

263
00:22:19,292 --> 00:22:21,669
It's not just a shame.
It's a huge letdown.

264
00:22:21,753 --> 00:22:23,505
We'll have to redirect the audience
to the livestream.

265
00:22:23,588 --> 00:22:24,881
I know this is far from ideal

266
00:22:24,964 --> 00:22:27,634
but keeping our promise
to the partner brands takes priority.

267
00:22:28,635 --> 00:22:29,761
You're right.

268
00:22:31,012 --> 00:22:32,722
How about projection mapping?

269
00:22:34,224 --> 00:22:35,517
Director Lee?

270
00:22:37,310 --> 00:22:39,813
Every brand in this show has
its own concept, right?

271
00:22:39,896 --> 00:22:42,190
We could visualize their keywords

272
00:22:42,482 --> 00:22:44,234
and shift the space's mood.

273
00:22:44,317 --> 00:22:46,778
The models would be walking
in the same studio

274
00:22:46,861 --> 00:22:49,197
but the background
would constantly feel new.

275
00:22:50,156 --> 00:22:53,409
You mean, use the white walls
as screens for a stage?

276
00:22:53,493 --> 00:22:54,702
Right.

277
00:22:55,036 --> 00:22:58,581
That would bring out
each brand's vibe much better.

278
00:23:06,214 --> 00:23:07,549
Can we prepare that in a day?

279
00:23:07,632 --> 00:23:09,676
I have a few references on hand.

280
00:23:10,969 --> 00:23:12,637
Shall we start
matching the outfits then?

281
00:23:13,012 --> 00:23:15,265
Good. Let's get things prepared
as soon as possible

282
00:23:15,348 --> 00:23:17,183
and run another rehearsal tonight.

283
00:23:18,935 --> 00:23:19,978
Let's get to work right away.

284
00:23:20,061 --> 00:23:22,689
- Yes, sir.
- Clear things out quickly.

285
00:23:22,772 --> 00:23:24,274
We're out of time.
Let's pick up the pace.

286
00:23:24,357 --> 00:23:26,442
Looks like we need
to clear this entire area.

287
00:23:27,485 --> 00:23:29,362
Be careful.

288
00:23:29,654 --> 00:23:30,697
One moment.

289
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:32,323
<i>Sales and Logistics,
prioritize setting up</i>

290
00:23:32,407 --> 00:23:34,492
<i>- the online show equipment.</i>
- Where are you going? Take these.

291
00:23:38,413 --> 00:23:39,622
This concept is too dark.

292
00:23:40,290 --> 00:23:42,667
<i>Planning and Merchandising,
back up Director Lee.</i>

293
00:23:42,834 --> 00:23:44,502
- A bit...
<i>- Get him</i>

294
00:23:44,586 --> 00:23:47,213
<i>whatever feedback,
info, or items he needs.</i>

295
00:23:48,965 --> 00:23:51,092
Hello, sir. We're doing
an online fashion show...

296
00:23:51,384 --> 00:23:53,136
<i>Marketing, you'll be the busiest.</i>

297
00:23:53,469 --> 00:23:55,179
<i>Announce the transition</i>

298
00:23:55,263 --> 00:23:57,724
<i>across all official Appello socials</i>

299
00:23:57,807 --> 00:23:59,726
<i>and notify the partner brands.</i>

300
00:24:00,518 --> 00:24:02,854
<i>Pull keywords for each brand too.</i>

301
00:24:04,647 --> 00:24:06,608
Ms. Kim, the notice is up
on the website.

302
00:24:06,691 --> 00:24:08,234
- Okay.
- The keyword visual aid is done too.

303
00:24:08,318 --> 00:24:10,570
Ms. Da-reum, run that over
to the studio quickly.

304
00:24:10,653 --> 00:24:11,654
Yes, ma'am.

305
00:24:14,157 --> 00:24:15,283
Here you go.

306
00:24:25,418 --> 00:24:27,629
That's our Director Chan.

307
00:24:27,712 --> 00:24:28,796
I like it.

308
00:24:29,380 --> 00:24:30,715
Add sunglasses to this look.

309
00:24:32,258 --> 00:24:33,468
He's so cool.

310
00:24:37,722 --> 00:24:40,558
<i>I hear you're diving
into the fashion business.</i>

311
00:24:40,642 --> 00:24:42,936
<i>Yes. Going forward,
I plan to incorporate the philosophy</i>

312
00:24:43,227 --> 00:24:45,480
<i>of "Unframe,"
which is to break out of the box.</i>

313
00:24:46,439 --> 00:24:49,275
<i>Stiff and standardized fashion
is boring.</i>

314
00:24:50,693 --> 00:24:54,364
I'd really love
to work with him someday.

315
00:24:54,572 --> 00:24:57,825
<i>Everyone dresses similarly
these days.</i>

316
00:24:57,909 --> 00:25:00,495
<i>Even the standards
for being fashionable are similar.</i>

317
00:25:00,578 --> 00:25:03,456
{\an8}<i>I want to shatter those standards.</i>

318
00:25:11,297 --> 00:25:13,257
We're actually working together now.

319
00:25:18,137 --> 00:25:19,389
It's crazy.

320
00:25:34,612 --> 00:25:37,865
Gosh. I heard you were out there
since dawn cleaning up the site.

321
00:25:37,949 --> 00:25:39,492
I didn't even think of that.

322
00:25:39,701 --> 00:25:40,743
The CEO is different indeed.

323
00:25:42,245 --> 00:25:43,746
Even our newest employee was there.

324
00:25:45,665 --> 00:25:47,417
- I see.
- Okay.

325
00:25:48,835 --> 00:25:51,170
Was she too busy to call me?

326
00:25:52,422 --> 00:25:53,548
- What?
- What?

327
00:25:54,215 --> 00:25:55,216
Nothing.

328
00:25:55,758 --> 00:25:58,928
Whoever it is, their dedication
to the company is remarkable.

329
00:25:59,637 --> 00:26:02,223
- We'll refer to this.
- Okay.

330
00:26:02,432 --> 00:26:03,474
- Thank you.
- No problem.

331
00:26:04,183 --> 00:26:06,060
I think so.

332
00:26:09,147 --> 00:26:10,565
Anyway, tomorrow is the problem.

333
00:26:10,940 --> 00:26:12,483
I have to head out
for a shoot right now.

334
00:26:13,276 --> 00:26:16,362
I'll take care
of the fashion show somehow.

335
00:26:18,573 --> 00:26:20,158
- Let's work this out.
- Okay.

336
00:26:20,241 --> 00:26:21,826
- See you.
- Bye. Let's be in touch.

337
00:26:27,582 --> 00:26:29,417
Wait, Chan is leaving.

338
00:26:45,892 --> 00:26:48,186
Was I gazing happily at Chan
in this mess?

339
00:26:48,519 --> 00:26:50,563
Jeez, I look like an absolute wreck.

340
00:26:54,734 --> 00:26:56,194
MOM

341
00:26:56,944 --> 00:26:59,030
- Aren't you having lunch?
- Let me step out briefly.

342
00:26:59,447 --> 00:27:01,240
- Goodness.
- Gosh, excuse me.

343
00:27:05,369 --> 00:27:06,704
Taxi.

344
00:27:10,416 --> 00:27:11,459
SE CORPORATION

345
00:27:13,628 --> 00:27:16,714
ONLY YOU, PARK SEO-JIN

346
00:27:18,299 --> 00:27:20,718
Please drive a little faster.
Thank you.

347
00:27:24,097 --> 00:27:25,306
It's Mom.

348
00:27:32,271 --> 00:27:34,023
Jeez, this is crazy.

349
00:27:36,734 --> 00:27:37,860
Mom!

350
00:27:38,945 --> 00:27:40,738
- Mom.
- Da-reum?

351
00:27:41,364 --> 00:27:42,740
What brings you here?

352
00:27:42,824 --> 00:27:45,993
I came to see my daughter, of course.

353
00:27:47,370 --> 00:27:49,705
- Come with me.
- What?

354
00:27:52,208 --> 00:27:55,711
You can't just drop by like this
without giving me a heads-up.

355
00:27:56,629 --> 00:27:58,589
Wait, Da-reum.

356
00:28:00,133 --> 00:28:02,009
Do you go to work dressed like that?

357
00:28:02,093 --> 00:28:03,177
Why?

358
00:28:04,053 --> 00:28:07,849
Jeez, you're frumpy and messy.

359
00:28:07,932 --> 00:28:09,142
Look at yourself.

360
00:28:09,267 --> 00:28:12,019
I don't normally dress this poorly.

361
00:28:13,146 --> 00:28:14,939
Something came up.

362
00:28:15,273 --> 00:28:16,816
Anyway, go now.

363
00:28:17,108 --> 00:28:18,442
You're good
now that you saw me, right?

364
00:28:18,818 --> 00:28:21,779
- Go on and leave.
- What... Wait.

365
00:28:21,863 --> 00:28:22,947
Wait up.

366
00:28:23,573 --> 00:28:24,615
Take this.

367
00:28:26,742 --> 00:28:29,787
You didn't have to bring this.
It's heavy.

368
00:28:30,121 --> 00:28:32,540
It's your favorite <i>jangjorim</i>.

369
00:28:33,416 --> 00:28:34,709
I packed just a little for you.

370
00:28:36,794 --> 00:28:38,379
What about the rice cakes
I sent the other day?

371
00:28:38,754 --> 00:28:40,381
Did you share them
with your coworkers?

372
00:28:40,756 --> 00:28:41,841
What did they say?

373
00:28:42,592 --> 00:28:44,635
Well, they...

374
00:28:44,969 --> 00:28:46,012
They loved them.

375
00:28:46,345 --> 00:28:48,472
Right?

376
00:28:48,556 --> 00:28:53,186
I lined up at a famous rice cake shop
from 5 a.m. just to order those.

377
00:28:56,772 --> 00:28:58,191
Mom, I...

378
00:28:59,108 --> 00:29:01,903
The truth is, SE Corporation...

379
00:29:17,835 --> 00:29:20,379
What is it?
Has work been tough lately?

380
00:29:23,507 --> 00:29:24,800
That's not it.

381
00:29:28,304 --> 00:29:30,306
That's how corporate life is.

382
00:29:31,557 --> 00:29:32,642
It's hard on everyone.

383
00:29:35,311 --> 00:29:38,272
But you know
I'm always rooting for you, right?

384
00:29:43,361 --> 00:29:44,445
Mom.

385
00:29:45,279 --> 00:29:46,280
I'm sorry.

386
00:29:48,449 --> 00:29:49,742
Oh, hush now.

387
00:29:50,201 --> 00:29:51,535
I should get going.

388
00:29:51,619 --> 00:29:53,037
It's almost time for my bus.

389
00:29:53,955 --> 00:29:55,665
Let me walk with you.
I'll catch you a cab.

390
00:29:56,624 --> 00:29:59,835
I met the CEO of BRB.

391
00:29:59,919 --> 00:30:02,880
He already signed with SE.

392
00:30:03,839 --> 00:30:06,008
Darn SE.

393
00:30:06,092 --> 00:30:08,886
I wish this building
would just collapse.

394
00:30:22,817 --> 00:30:26,070
- What's wrong?
<i>- Hold on. Let me send you something.</i>

395
00:30:26,153 --> 00:30:27,280
I'm hanging up.

396
00:30:30,324 --> 00:30:31,701
- Thank you.
- What...

397
00:30:32,994 --> 00:30:34,412
You work at SE, right?

398
00:30:34,495 --> 00:30:36,789
I'm running late for an appointment.
Take this.

399
00:30:36,872 --> 00:30:37,915
Here.

400
00:30:39,959 --> 00:30:41,877
- What...
- Wait a second.

401
00:30:41,961 --> 00:30:43,462
Is that how you dress at work?

402
00:30:43,879 --> 00:30:45,214
What do you do with your paycheck?

403
00:30:45,298 --> 00:30:47,466
Dress up a little, okay?

404
00:30:48,718 --> 00:30:49,927
What the...

405
00:30:50,011 --> 00:30:51,345
Let's go.

406
00:30:52,096 --> 00:30:53,556
But that's my taxi.

407
00:31:01,439 --> 00:31:02,732
This is outrageous.

408
00:31:07,361 --> 00:31:08,904
COCOTALK

409
00:31:08,988 --> 00:31:11,115
TEAM MANAGER CHOI SEONG-WOOK

410
00:31:13,659 --> 00:31:14,910
<i>This is Ms. Nam Da-reum, right?</i>

411
00:31:15,411 --> 00:31:17,413
<i>She's not secretly meeting
Director Kim of SE, is she?</i>

412
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,691
Where's Ms. Nam?

413
00:31:45,775 --> 00:31:48,235
She stepped out saying,
"Let me step out briefly."

414
00:32:02,458 --> 00:32:04,585
- Ms. Nam.
- Yes?

415
00:32:04,668 --> 00:32:05,878
Where have you been?

416
00:32:06,629 --> 00:32:09,382
I had urgent business

417
00:32:09,465 --> 00:32:11,258
so I stepped out briefly
during lunch.

418
00:32:11,342 --> 00:32:12,468
What kind of business?

419
00:32:13,302 --> 00:32:16,389
Well...

420
00:32:20,101 --> 00:32:21,310
Well...

421
00:32:21,477 --> 00:32:23,813
A friend wanted to see me real quick.

422
00:32:25,064 --> 00:32:27,608
I don't know what you've been
going around getting

423
00:32:27,691 --> 00:32:29,485
but it's a basic rule
to report when leaving the office

424
00:32:29,568 --> 00:32:31,737
even during a lunch break.
Don't you know that?

425
00:32:31,821 --> 00:32:33,030
Is the company a joke to you?

426
00:32:37,410 --> 00:32:38,702
I apologize.

427
00:32:43,791 --> 00:32:45,459
Listen up, new hires.

428
00:32:45,543 --> 00:32:46,752
Stop assisting for the fashion show

429
00:32:47,211 --> 00:32:49,255
and go back to your regular duties.

430
00:32:49,338 --> 00:32:50,798
We've got things under control now.

431
00:32:50,881 --> 00:32:52,508
And the office needs a skeleton crew.

432
00:32:55,177 --> 00:32:56,429
Mr. Kang.

433
00:32:58,097 --> 00:33:01,100
Can't I help with the show
until the end?

434
00:33:01,684 --> 00:33:03,519
I've been on this
since the rehearsals.

435
00:33:03,769 --> 00:33:06,021
I want to see it through.

436
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,401
Ms. Nam.

437
00:33:11,944 --> 00:33:13,362
Didn't you hear me?

438
00:33:16,449 --> 00:33:17,616
Stay out of it.

439
00:33:35,134 --> 00:33:37,219
Mr. Kang is too harsh.

440
00:33:38,596 --> 00:33:42,892
I mean, you cared enough to rush out
to the site at the crack of dawn.

441
00:33:43,517 --> 00:33:45,311
Are you okay, Ms. Da-reum?

442
00:33:46,604 --> 00:33:47,938
I'm all right.

443
00:33:48,022 --> 00:33:51,484
We're promoting it on socials
and pop-up windows

444
00:33:51,567 --> 00:33:52,693
but how many will actually see it?

445
00:33:53,110 --> 00:33:54,361
Exactly.

446
00:33:54,778 --> 00:33:56,780
Don't you get the feeling

447
00:33:56,864 --> 00:34:00,576
that the online fashion show
is going to flop quietly?

448
00:34:00,659 --> 00:34:01,911
What do we do?

449
00:34:13,255 --> 00:34:14,298
Guys.

450
00:34:16,008 --> 00:34:17,343
Why don't we try doing something?

451
00:34:27,686 --> 00:34:28,687
- Oh, wow.
- Oh, wow.

452
00:34:32,191 --> 00:34:33,943
Ms. Da-reum, you're good at it.

453
00:34:34,026 --> 00:34:36,445
Why do you care so much
about this show, Ms. Da-reum?

454
00:34:36,529 --> 00:34:39,782
Seeing everyone work so hard on-site
made me promise myself

455
00:34:40,866 --> 00:34:44,411
that I'd do my absolute best
to ensure this show's success.

456
00:34:45,663 --> 00:34:46,997
You're so cool.

457
00:34:47,623 --> 00:34:48,999
You can do it, Ms. Da-reum.

458
00:34:53,629 --> 00:34:59,301
<i>Time to put all my fangirl skills
to good use!</i>

459
00:34:59,385 --> 00:35:01,011
Could you make a few adjustments
to the model?

460
00:35:02,471 --> 00:35:04,557
The lighting's too bright
with too much glare on the clothes.

461
00:35:04,640 --> 00:35:05,891
Please adjust that as well.

462
00:35:06,183 --> 00:35:07,226
Will do.

463
00:35:07,851 --> 00:35:08,894
Mr. Kang.

464
00:35:10,354 --> 00:35:11,397
Take a look at this.

465
00:35:13,983 --> 00:35:15,109
<i>We went from this...</i>

466
00:35:15,192 --> 00:35:16,735
OUR FASHION SHOW IS ON AS PLANNED

467
00:35:16,819 --> 00:35:18,320
<i>...to this.</i>

468
00:35:19,488 --> 00:35:20,531
APPELLO IN NAMSAN

469
00:35:20,614 --> 00:35:22,866
OUR

470
00:35:22,950 --> 00:35:25,035
FASHION SHOW

471
00:35:25,244 --> 00:35:27,246
IS ON

472
00:35:27,746 --> 00:35:28,914
AS PLANNED

473
00:35:32,835 --> 00:35:34,545
TRADITION NEVER DIES

474
00:35:36,463 --> 00:35:38,007
THOSE DAYS, THAT FEEL

475
00:35:38,465 --> 00:35:41,135
WEAR CLOTHES OF TOMORROW

476
00:35:43,637 --> 00:35:44,888
NOVEMBER 13, 6:00 P.M., LIVE

477
00:35:45,347 --> 00:35:46,515
What is this?

478
00:35:46,599 --> 00:35:49,435
The rookies made it
to promote the online show.

479
00:35:49,810 --> 00:35:50,936
Isn't it fun?

480
00:35:51,020 --> 00:35:53,856
How about we post it
on our official account?

481
00:35:54,189 --> 00:35:55,190
It's fun.

482
00:35:55,774 --> 00:35:56,775
Whose idea was this?

483
00:35:57,359 --> 00:35:58,402
Nam Da-reum's.

484
00:36:00,571 --> 00:36:01,989
It was Ms. Nam's?

485
00:36:02,448 --> 00:36:03,449
Yes.

486
00:36:04,908 --> 00:36:05,909
Ms. Kim.

487
00:36:06,493 --> 00:36:09,872
Did Ms. Da-reum
handle any sensitive info

488
00:36:09,955 --> 00:36:11,248
regarding the fashion show?

489
00:36:11,790 --> 00:36:13,042
No.

490
00:36:13,125 --> 00:36:16,045
We don't put a rookie in charge
of anything too important.

491
00:36:16,879 --> 00:36:18,589
Why? Is there a problem?

492
00:36:20,966 --> 00:36:21,967
Come with me.

493
00:36:27,848 --> 00:36:29,642
There's something I didn't tell you.

494
00:36:29,975 --> 00:36:31,018
Yes?

495
00:36:37,274 --> 00:36:38,359
Ms. Da-reum.

496
00:36:40,611 --> 00:36:42,363
She worked at SE Corporation.

497
00:36:44,406 --> 00:36:45,491
Yes, I know that.

498
00:36:46,909 --> 00:36:48,869
- You knew that?
- Yes.

499
00:36:48,952 --> 00:36:51,080
She told me she used to work there.

500
00:36:51,163 --> 00:36:52,706
It wasn't on her resume.

501
00:36:53,624 --> 00:36:56,960
She was there for under two months
and thought it would look bad.

502
00:36:57,670 --> 00:36:58,962
She couldn't stand the place

503
00:36:59,046 --> 00:37:01,882
and waited for us
to post about a vacancy.

504
00:37:03,175 --> 00:37:05,094
She didn't even tell her family yet.

505
00:37:05,260 --> 00:37:08,639
Her mom went to SE Corporation
to bring her a lunch box today.

506
00:37:11,809 --> 00:37:12,810
Where are you coming from?

507
00:37:34,456 --> 00:37:37,876
Mr. Kang reviewed the clip you made.

508
00:37:37,960 --> 00:37:39,878
Regarding uploading it
to our official account...

509
00:37:45,384 --> 00:37:47,094
it's a go!

510
00:37:50,556 --> 00:37:53,851
He told me to tell you
you did so well.

511
00:37:54,935 --> 00:37:58,897
Plus, you can all help out
with tomorrow's fashion show.

512
00:38:00,107 --> 00:38:01,400
Can we really?

513
00:38:02,776 --> 00:38:06,613
Post that video on our account,
then go home.

514
00:38:07,156 --> 00:38:08,824
- Okay!
- Thank you.

515
00:38:08,907 --> 00:38:10,242
You did so well.

516
00:38:10,325 --> 00:38:11,535
- Thank you!
- Thank you.

517
00:38:11,618 --> 00:38:12,661
Bye.

518
00:38:21,670 --> 00:38:22,713
Come on.

519
00:38:23,088 --> 00:38:24,173
Let's go upstairs.

520
00:38:30,429 --> 00:38:32,222
- Hyeok.
- Hey.

521
00:38:32,556 --> 00:38:33,974
- You go ahead.
- Okay.

522
00:38:34,600 --> 00:38:35,642
It's been so long.

523
00:38:36,602 --> 00:38:38,395
- Do you have a shoot?
- Sorry?

524
00:38:39,021 --> 00:38:40,981
I was invited on a variety show.

525
00:38:41,356 --> 00:38:43,609
- To do what?
- A bit of this and that.

526
00:38:44,193 --> 00:38:45,194
That's great.

