Here you go.

794
00:59:31,147 --> 00:59:35,026
DA-REUM

795
00:59:39,572 --> 00:59:40,781
It's so strange.

796
00:59:40,865 --> 00:59:42,199
What is?

797
00:59:42,783 --> 00:59:43,868
That I'm

798
00:59:44,452 --> 00:59:47,371
sitting here, chatting with you.

799
00:59:54,003 --> 00:59:55,588
I think it's strange how we met.

800
00:59:55,671 --> 00:59:56,756
Why is that?

801
00:59:58,632 --> 01:00:01,302
I'm just one of your many fans.

802
01:00:01,385 --> 01:00:03,220
I may have many fans

803
01:00:03,471 --> 01:00:04,889
but I don't meet them all like this.

804
01:00:05,306 --> 01:00:06,682
I don't have the chance to.

805
01:00:09,769 --> 01:00:11,270
I see.

806
01:00:13,564 --> 01:00:15,900
I'd like to know
how you became my fan.

807
01:00:17,151 --> 01:00:19,361
- How?
- Yes, how.

808
01:00:23,574 --> 01:00:25,284
{\an8}HAPPY BIRTHDAY, NAM DA-REUM

809
01:00:42,009 --> 01:00:43,135
Let's get a pastry.

810
01:00:43,219 --> 01:00:44,428
- I'll buy you one.
- Great.

811
01:00:44,512 --> 01:00:45,554
- You will?
- Yes.

812
01:00:46,013 --> 01:00:47,556
Can I eat more than one?

813
01:00:51,435 --> 01:00:54,021
<i>What were you like
in high school, Chan?</i>

814
01:00:54,105 --> 01:00:55,272
<i>In high school?</i>

815
01:00:57,316 --> 01:01:00,069
<i>I didn't stand out. I was quiet.</i>

816
01:01:00,152 --> 01:01:03,906
<i>Before I knew it, I was invisible.</i>

817
01:01:05,533 --> 01:01:07,535
<i>People acted like I wasn't there</i>

818
01:01:07,910 --> 01:01:10,704
<i>and that was harder
than actually being bullied.</i>

819
01:01:11,080 --> 01:01:13,332
If someone had said
just one word to me

820
01:01:13,791 --> 01:01:15,459
going to school would've hurt less.

821
01:01:23,384 --> 01:01:26,512
<i>If anyone out there
is going through the same thing</i>

822
01:01:27,721 --> 01:01:28,848
<i>I hope they remember this.</i>

823
01:01:30,933 --> 01:01:32,518
You may feel alone right now

824
01:01:33,894 --> 01:01:35,396
but someone will appear one day

825
01:01:36,105 --> 01:01:37,273
to love you.

826
01:01:39,275 --> 01:01:40,442
They did for me.

827
01:01:43,195 --> 01:01:44,321
<i>Until then</i>

828
01:01:46,157 --> 01:01:47,783
<i>I want to tell them to hang in there.</i>

829
01:01:49,243 --> 01:01:50,619
<i>That's my message.</i>

830
01:02:17,646 --> 01:02:18,689
Hi.

831
01:02:26,280 --> 01:02:29,283
Do you like D.N.X too?

832
01:02:34,121 --> 01:02:35,164
Yes.

833
01:02:36,415 --> 01:02:38,667
Nice to meet you, comrade.

834
01:02:40,336 --> 01:02:41,670
Okay, so...

835
01:02:42,379 --> 01:02:44,006
My D.N.X bias

836
01:02:44,965 --> 01:02:47,051
is Roy. Who is your favorite?

837
01:02:47,134 --> 01:02:49,261
Just so you know, I love Hyeok.

838
01:02:52,264 --> 01:02:53,307
My bias

839
01:02:54,058 --> 01:02:55,100
is Lee Chan.

840
01:02:55,351 --> 01:02:57,645
- It's Lee Chan.
- We don't overlap.

841
01:02:57,728 --> 01:02:59,563
That's why you have his merch.

842
01:02:59,647 --> 01:03:02,900
Hey, isn't this really rare?

843
01:03:02,983 --> 01:03:04,818
Can I have a look?

844
01:03:07,363 --> 01:03:09,823
- Yes.
- Oh, wow. Thanks.

845
01:03:11,867 --> 01:03:13,118
- Look!
- It's so cute.

846
01:03:13,786 --> 01:03:16,205
It's so cute.

847
01:03:16,288 --> 01:03:18,040
My gosh. It's adorable.

848
01:03:18,874 --> 01:03:21,043
Look at this. I wish I had this.

849
01:03:23,170 --> 01:03:27,258
They are my best friends to this day.

850
01:03:31,887 --> 01:03:33,264
That must've been so tough.

851
01:03:37,017 --> 01:03:41,605
Your songs got me
through my worst times.

852
01:03:41,855 --> 01:03:44,692
And they brought
my best friends to me

853
01:03:44,775 --> 01:03:47,194
so I could enjoy
the rest of high school.

854
01:03:47,778 --> 01:03:48,779
That's why

855
01:03:50,114 --> 01:03:51,907
I'm always grateful to you.

856
01:03:57,371 --> 01:03:58,580
You held up well.

857
01:04:00,249 --> 01:04:01,292
And grew up well.

858
01:04:16,181 --> 01:04:17,266
But

859
01:04:18,267 --> 01:04:19,351
is that it?

860
01:04:20,394 --> 01:04:22,062
There could be other reasons.

861
01:04:22,438 --> 01:04:25,274
My good looks. My cool persona.

862
01:04:25,566 --> 01:04:26,775
My charms.

863
01:04:26,859 --> 01:04:28,319
That's a give...

864
01:04:30,612 --> 01:04:31,864
It's a given.

865
01:04:33,782 --> 01:04:37,036
There's no one else like you
with such perfect looks

866
01:04:37,119 --> 01:04:38,746
and a great character.

867
01:04:40,039 --> 01:04:41,915
That's what I'm like on TV.

868
01:04:43,667 --> 01:04:45,294
I could be completely different.

869
01:04:47,421 --> 01:04:49,048
I could be fake.

870
01:04:50,382 --> 01:04:51,800
I could be a hypocrite.

871
01:04:54,053 --> 01:04:56,972
You are a good person.

872
01:05:02,061 --> 01:05:05,439
I adored you for 12 years.
I can tell that much.

873
01:05:08,400 --> 01:05:11,528
If you tried to be
a good person so far

874
01:05:12,738 --> 01:05:15,824
that alone makes you a good person.

875
01:05:22,164 --> 01:05:24,083
Long-standing fans are grateful

876
01:05:24,166 --> 01:05:27,044
that you didn't get into any trouble.

877
01:05:27,211 --> 01:05:31,548
You didn't drink and drive or gamble.

878
01:05:33,425 --> 01:05:34,468
I mean it.

879
01:05:35,928 --> 01:05:39,932
I'm really so proud of you.

880
01:05:41,266 --> 01:05:42,976
Are you? Thanks.

881
01:05:52,236 --> 01:05:53,237
Thank you.

882
01:06:16,844 --> 01:06:19,179
No, it's not messy. I was gentle.

883
01:06:19,263 --> 01:06:20,514
Are you sure?

884
01:06:20,597 --> 01:06:21,682
I'll do it.

885
01:06:21,890 --> 01:06:23,058
It's better.

886
01:06:27,563 --> 01:06:29,148
I had it taken care of.

887
01:06:32,568 --> 01:06:34,236
- Chan.
- What?

888
01:06:35,028 --> 01:06:36,572
Keep it a secret that I'm your fan.

889
01:06:36,864 --> 01:06:39,116
- All of a sudden?
- Please...

890
01:06:40,826 --> 01:06:41,994
Then grant me a wish.

891
01:06:42,202 --> 01:06:45,038
What? Okay, fine, whatever.

892
01:06:47,374 --> 01:06:49,626
I'll think of a wish, Da-reum.

893
01:06:52,838 --> 01:06:53,922
Okay?

894
01:07:01,430 --> 01:07:02,473
"Da-reum"?

895
01:07:22,659 --> 01:07:26,580
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

896
01:07:37,758 --> 01:07:39,801
{\an8}EPILOGUE

897
01:07:39,885 --> 01:07:40,969
{\an8}Hey, Chan.

898
01:07:41,386 --> 01:07:43,555
We got the theme for the photoshoot.

899
01:07:43,639 --> 01:07:44,723
I'm tired.

900
01:07:44,806 --> 01:07:45,933
Don't you need a look?

901
01:07:46,934 --> 01:07:49,061
These are the questions for when

902
01:07:49,144 --> 01:07:51,271
- you meet your fans...
- Later.

903
01:07:51,355 --> 01:07:52,356
Okay.

904
01:07:54,900 --> 01:07:57,486
- If you're in a bad mood...
- I'm tired and you're noisy.

905
01:08:02,533 --> 01:08:06,078
I think an actor
should check this out.

906
01:08:06,495 --> 01:08:08,121
That would help.

907
01:08:08,622 --> 01:08:10,958
That's how you become successful.

908
01:08:15,754 --> 01:08:17,005
FASHION SHOW IS ON

909
01:08:18,715 --> 01:08:19,758
AS PLANNED

910
01:08:23,262 --> 01:08:26,557
- Hey.
- What is it?

911
01:08:28,058 --> 01:08:29,226
Let's film a challenge video.

912
01:08:29,977 --> 01:08:32,354
You just said you were tired.

913
01:08:32,854 --> 01:08:35,190
- We must do it now.
- Right now?

914
01:08:35,274 --> 01:08:39,027
Action. One, two, three.

915
01:08:40,571 --> 01:08:42,197
<i>You're moving way too fast.</i>

916
01:08:42,281 --> 01:08:44,199
<i>Slow down.</i>

917
01:08:51,582 --> 01:08:53,709
Let's try that once more.

918
01:08:55,335 --> 01:08:56,420
Let's do this.

919
01:08:58,297 --> 01:08:59,339
{\an8}SPECIAL THANKS TO CHANG HYAE-JIN,
HUR JUNG-DO, AN YOUNG-MI

920
01:08:59,423 --> 01:09:02,134
{\an8}Don't be so weak.
You're carrying your Chan.

921
01:09:02,759 --> 01:09:03,802
{\an8}<i>Are you jealous?</i>

922
01:09:04,469 --> 01:09:06,763
{\an8}<i>We're at work.
I'm worried people will talk.</i>

923
01:09:07,472 --> 01:09:09,850
{\an8}A date? What should I do?

924
01:09:09,933 --> 01:09:12,477
{\an8}<i>Is it a gift for someone you like?</i>

925
01:09:13,729 --> 01:09:15,022
{\an8}<i>Let's go to my place.</i>

926
01:09:15,105 --> 01:09:17,149
{\an8}<i>Will you go as a woman or as a fan?</i>

927
01:09:19,318 --> 01:09:20,694
{\an8}No! Ms. Nam!

928
01:09:21,069 --> 01:09:23,196
{\an8}That she likes me.

929
01:09:23,739 --> 01:09:24,906
{\an8}<i>A head-on</i>

930
01:09:26,116 --> 01:09:27,242
{\an8}<i>romance?</i>

